square.\n\n5. **B: f1-c4** - Develops the bishop actively toward Black\'s weak f7 square.\n\nReason:\nThe best move is **P: e4-f5**. While accepting a gambit can be risky, in this position the material gain is significant and Black doesn\'t have sufficient compensation. After capturing on f5, I\'m up a full pawn, and Black\'s supposed "activity" is limited since their pieces are still undeveloped. The f-file isn\'t immediately useful to Black, and I can consolidate my extra pawn with moves like d4, Nf3, and normal development. Declining with e5 or d4 gives Black exactly the dynamic play they\'re seeking from the gambit.\n\nAnswer: P: e4-f5'}
