lack would need to move a piece to control g8. After g6xh7, I'm also threatening h7-h8 promotion, and I've removed a defender.\n\nReason: I choose **P: g6-h7** because:\n- It captures Black's h7 pawn, gaining material\n- It maintains the immediate promotion threat (h7-h8 next turn)\n- The h-file is less defended than the g-file (no Black rook directly opposing)\n- This forces Black to respond to the promotion threat while I've already gained a pawn\n\nAnswer: P: g6-h7"}
