t promotion choice.\n\nOther moves like developing pieces (N: b1-c3, N: g1-f3) or advancing central pawns (d2-d4, e2... wait, e2 is occupied by my king apparently) are reasonable but pale in comparison to gaining a queen.\n\nReason:\nPromoting to a queen on g8 gives me an overwhelming material advantage (9 points of material). The queen will be actively placed, potentially threatening Black's king on e8 and controlling key squares. This is a forcing move that immediately changes the evaluation of the position in my favor. There's no reason to delay this promotion or choose a weaker piece.\n\nAnswer: P: h7-g8-q"}
