ntral squares.\n\n4. **P: d2-d4** - Classical central pawn move, fighting for the center.\n\nReason:\nI choose **Q: d1-h5** because:\n- Black's king on f7 is critically exposed and cannot castle\n- Qh5+ gives check, forcing Black's king to move and further disrupting their position\n- This forcing move puts immediate pressure on Black before they can consolidate their unusual position\n- After Qh5+, Black's king will be even more exposed, and White can follow up with rapid development while maintaining the initiative\n- The tactical opportunity presented by the misplaced king is too significant to pass up for slower developmental moves\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-h5"}
