), very strong.\n\nThe key tactical shots are:\n- **Q: h5-e8** gives check, and after the King moves (likely Kd6, Kf6, or Kd5), I maintain pressure\n- **Q: h5-e5** also gives check directly to the King on e6\n\nReason: Q: h5-e8 is the most forcing move, delivering check to the exposed Black King. After this check, Black's King must move to an even more awkward square (likely d6, d5, f6, or f5), and I can continue to harass it while developing my pieces. The King on e6 is a severe positional weakness, and this check exploits it maximally. This maintains my initiative and prevents Black from consolidating their position.\n\nAnswer: Q: h5-e8"}
