e threats.\n\n4. **K: e1-g1** - Castling for king safety is generally good, but with Black's king so exposed, I should look for forcing moves first.\n\nReason:\nN: f3-e5 is clearly the strongest move. It:\n- Directly attacks the exposed Black king on d6\n- The knight on e5 would be protected by the d2 pawn (if I advance it) and cannot be easily challenged\n- Forces Black into a defensive position\n- Creates multiple threats including potential discovered attacks with my bishop\n- Exploits Black's biggest weakness: the centralized, exposed king\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
