* - Developing central control but passive given the tactical opportunity.\n\nReason: The move **N: e5-d7** is clearly the strongest. It places the knight on a superb outpost where it:\n- Gives check to the Black king on d6, forcing it to move\n- Controls critical central squares (b6, b8, c5, e5, f6, f8)\n- Cannot be easily dislodged\n- Maximizes pressure on Black's awkward piece coordination\n- The exposed Black king will struggle to find safety while I maintain initiative\n\nThis is a classic example of exploiting a misplaced king with active piece play.\n\nAnswer: N: e5-d7"}
