e forcing moves that limit the opponent's options and often lead to tactical advantages. After the King moves, I can potentially reposition my Knight to an even better square or coordinate with my Bishop for further threats. This forcing move maintains the initiative and puts maximum pressure on Black's exposed King position.\n\nAnswer: N: d7-f6"}
