ed Black king on d6, and simultaneously attacks the Black queen on d7. This is a classic royal fork pattern. Black must move the king to escape check (since blocking or capturing the bishop on d7 is impossible with the queen standing there), and then I capture the queen on the next move, winning decisive material. This tactical blow should lead to an easy victory.\n\nAnswer: B: c6-d7"}
