idate my position and potentially coordinate an attack.\n\nReason: B: d7-a4 delivers check to the exposed Black king on c5, forcing Black to respond to the threat immediately. This gives me initiative and time to improve my position. After Black moves the king, I can continue developing while maintaining pressure. The bishop on a4 also controls important central squares and keeps Black's king uncomfortable.\n\nAnswer: B: d7-a4"}
