ssure.\n\nThe most forcing move is **R: c8-a8**, which delivers check to the Black king on a5.\n\nReason: Checking the opponent's king is almost always the first priority to evaluate. R: c8-a8 gives check, forcing Black's king to move. The king's options will be limited: it cannot go to a4 (attacked by my bishop on b5), cannot stay on a5, and must move to b4 or b5. If Kb5, my bishop must move but I maintain pressure. If Kb4, I can continue harassing the exposed king. This forcing move gives me the initiative and puts Black on the defensive, which is crucial in an endgame.\n\nAnswer: R: c8-a8"}
