h my other pieces\n- Black's bishop would be forced to move, losing coordination\n\nReason: N: d5-c7 is the strongest move. It puts immediate pressure on Black's bishop while the knight occupies an excellent outpost on c7. This forces Black into a defensive position where they must deal with the threat to their bishop. Given my material advantage, active piece play that improves my position while restricting Black's options is the key to converting this win.\n\nAnswer: N: d5-c7"}
