Black King and win the Black pawns or deliver checkmate.\n\n**R: a1-b1** is excellent because it attacks the King on b4 and forces it to move (since it would give check). This activates my Rook powerfully.\n\nActually, wait - if the King is on b4, then R: a1-b1 would put the King in check along the b-file. This forces Black\'s King to move and gives me control of the b-file.\n\nReason: R: a1-b1 gives check to the Black King on b4, forcing it to move. This activates my most powerful piece (the Rook) and seizes control of the b-file, which will help restrict Black\'s King and win Black\'s pawns. This is the most forcing and strongest move in the position.\n\nAnswer: R: a1-b1'}
