ve because:\n- It places the rook on the 7th rank (the second-to-last rank from Black's perspective), which is a dominant position\n- It gives check to the black king on c7, forcing it to move to a worse square\n- It restricts the black king's mobility significantly\n- After the king moves, I can continue to dominate with my material advantage and work toward promoting pawns or capturing the black pawn\n\nAnswer: R: b6-b7"}
