ay **K: c6-d6** to maintain king activity and keep Black's king restricted. The more active my king, the better my chances to create threats. This move keeps the Black king confined while maintaining maximum flexibility for my other pieces. With the Black king trapped on c8 or nearby squares, I can later coordinate my bishop and pawn advance more effectively.\n\nAnswer: K: c6-d6"}
